  "nl_text": "The database schema \"rschema_0423\" is used to store information about online courses, instructors, and students. It consists of seven tables: Course, Chapter, Instructor, Student, Course_material, Instructor_teaching, and Viewing_record.\nThe Course table contains information about each course, including its category, description, name, difficulty level, number of lessons, recommended status, target audience, and total duration. The Course_ID column is the primary key, and the table has a foreign key reference to the Chapter table.\nThe Chapter table contains information about each chapter in a course, including its description, name, duration, and video URL. The Chapter_ID column is the primary key, and the table has foreign key references to the Course and Chapter tables.\nThe Instructor table contains information about each instructor, including their avatar, name, personal profile, professional field, and teaching experience. The Instructor_ID column is the primary key, and the table has a foreign key reference to the Instructor_teaching table.\nThe Student table contains information about each student, including their account status, age, avatar, contact information, gender, membership level, name, points, registration time, and student ID. The Student_ID column is the primary key, and the table has foreign key references to the Viewing_record and Instructor_teaching tables.\nThe Course_material table contains information about each course material, including its course ID, material ID, material URL, and material name. The Course_ID column is the primary key, and the table has a foreign key reference to the Course table.\nThe Instructor_teaching table contains information about each instructor's teaching performance, including their course ID, instructor ID, rating, and student feedback. The primary key is a composite of the instructor ID and course ID, and the table has foreign key references to the Course and Instructor tables.\nThe Viewing_record table contains information about each student's viewing record, including their chapter ID, completion status, student ID, view count, and viewing duration. The primary key is a composite of the student ID and chapter ID, and the table has foreign key references to the Chapter and Student tables.\nOverall, this schema provides a comprehensive database for an online learning platform, allowing for the storage of course information, instructor information, student information, course materials, and viewing records.",
  "gold_question": "This is an online education platform's course management system. For course management, the system supports maintaining basic course information (course ID, course name, course description, etc.), records detailed course information (number of lessons, total duration, difficulty level, etc.), and manages course classification information (course category, target audience, recommendation status, etc.). For chapter management, the system maintains basic chapter information (chapter ID, chapter name, chapter description, etc.), records detailed chapter information (video URL, course materials, duration, etc.), and manages chapter sequence (previous/next chapters, chapter hierarchy, etc.). For instructor management, the system maintains basic instructor information (instructor ID, name, avatar, etc.), records detailed instructor information (teaching experience, professional field, personal profile, etc.), and manages instructor courses (teaching list, ratings, student feedback, etc.). For student management, the system maintains basic student information, including basic data (student ID, name, avatar, gender, age, contact information) and account information (registration time, account status, membership level, points), while tracking learning progress, including course progress (selected courses, current learning chapter, last learning time), viewing records (viewing duration per lesson, number of views, completion status) and learning statistics (total learning duration, course completion rate).",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0423.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0423\nCREATE TABLE `Course` (\n  `Course_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `category` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `difficulty_level` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `number_of_lessons` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `recommended_status` boolean DEFAULT NULL,\n  `target_audience` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `total_duration` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Course_ID`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Chapter` (\n  `Chapter_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `duration` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `video_url` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Course_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Chapter_ID`),\n  CONSTRAINT `Chapter_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`Course_ID`) REFERENCES `Course` (`Course_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Instructor` (\n  `Instructor_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `avatar` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `personal_profile` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `professional_field` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `teaching_experience` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Instructor_ID`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Student` (\n  `Student_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `account_status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `age` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `avatar` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `contact_information` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `gender` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `membership_level` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `points` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `registration_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Student_ID`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Course_material` (\n  `Course_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `material_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `material_url` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `material_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Course_ID`),\n  CONSTRAINT `Course_material_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`Course_ID`) REFERENCES `Course` (`Course_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Instructor_teaching` (\n  `Instructor_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Course_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `rating` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `student_feedback` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Instructor_ID`, `Course_ID`),\n  CONSTRAINT `Instructor_teaching_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`Instructor_ID`) REFERENCES `Instructor` (`Instructor_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `Instructor_teaching_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`Course_ID`) REFERENCES `Course` (`Course_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Viewing_record` (\n  `Student_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Chapter_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `completion_status` boolean DEFAULT NULL,\n  `view_count` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `viewing_duration` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Student_ID`, `Chapter_ID`),\n  CONSTRAINT `Viewing_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`Chapter_ID`) REFERENCES `Chapter` (`Chapter_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `Viewing_record_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`Student_ID`) REFERENCES `Student` (`Student_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
